WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.200
Lecturer: So another thing we can do

00:01.200 --> 00:03.990
if we're working on a repository with collaborators

00:03.990 --> 00:07.140
is add in branch protection rules.

00:07.140 --> 00:08.940
So, if we go into Settings,

00:08.940 --> 00:10.590
assuming that you are somebody

00:10.590 --> 00:12.210
who has access to settings

00:12.210 --> 00:13.320
on the repository,

00:13.320 --> 00:14.523
under Branches,

00:15.570 --> 00:16.620
we have, first of all,

00:16.620 --> 00:17.520
the default branch,

00:17.520 --> 00:18.720
you can configure this.

00:18.720 --> 00:20.070
So, if you want to make it,

00:20.070 --> 00:21.420
something else, for example,

00:21.420 --> 00:22.770
if you have main and master

00:22.770 --> 00:24.630
and you realize you only want main,

00:24.630 --> 00:25.530
to be the default,

00:25.530 --> 00:26.970
well, I shouldn't say only,

00:26.970 --> 00:28.620
you can only have one default.

00:28.620 --> 00:30.870
So, if you want to switch that to main,

00:30.870 --> 00:31.890
then you could do that here,

00:31.890 --> 00:34.170
but we already have main as ours.

00:34.170 --> 00:36.150
Or, if we needed to change it in some way,

00:36.150 --> 00:38.100
you can change that default branch.

00:38.100 --> 00:38.970
But then down here,

00:38.970 --> 00:41.220
it says branch protection rules.

00:41.220 --> 00:42.690
Define branch protection rules

00:42.690 --> 00:43.920
to disable force pushing,

00:43.920 --> 00:45.450
prevent branches from being deleted,

00:45.450 --> 00:48.600
and optionally require status checks before merging.

00:48.600 --> 00:50.880
New to branch protection rules, learn more.

00:50.880 --> 00:52.710
So, we're going to add a rule.

00:52.710 --> 00:54.420
We're gonna protect our main branch.

00:54.420 --> 00:55.253
The first thing it asks

00:55.253 --> 00:57.450
is for a branch name pattern.

00:57.450 --> 00:59.580
Now, instead of just a branch name,

00:59.580 --> 01:02.040
it gives us the option of putting a pattern in here

01:02.040 --> 01:04.200
because on large projects,

01:04.200 --> 01:06.870
there may be thousands of branches

01:06.870 --> 01:09.810
that are pushed up or pull requests generated from.

01:09.810 --> 01:13.260
And the organization or the project enforces rules

01:13.260 --> 01:14.240
where they need to be something like,

01:14.240 --> 01:19.240
/feature/blah or /release,

01:20.040 --> 01:21.870
if it's a big release of,

01:21.870 --> 01:23.010
I can't spell release,

01:23.010 --> 01:24.270
but there are different patterns

01:24.270 --> 01:25.800
you could define different rules

01:25.800 --> 01:27.810
for those different types of branches

01:27.810 --> 01:29.820
instead of having to name each one.

01:29.820 --> 01:31.110
But, we're not gonna do that.

01:31.110 --> 01:32.250
We only have our main branch.

01:32.250 --> 01:34.020
So, we'll just put main in there.

01:34.020 --> 01:35.550
And then, I'm gonna do this,

01:35.550 --> 01:39.210
require pull request reviews before merging.

01:39.210 --> 01:41.130
This means that our commits need to be made

01:41.130 --> 01:43.440
to a non-protected branch, basically,

01:43.440 --> 01:46.410
not main and then submitted via pull request.

01:46.410 --> 01:49.230
And then, at least one person which is, (chuckles)

01:49.230 --> 01:50.310
that we've only got two here,

01:50.310 --> 01:54.000
so, only one person needs to approve the PR

01:54.000 --> 01:55.590
before it can be merged.

01:55.590 --> 01:57.240
So, I just wanna demonstrate,

01:57.240 --> 01:58.073
how that would work.

01:58.073 --> 01:59.220
There are other things, right?

01:59.220 --> 02:00.690
Do we allow people to delete

02:00.690 --> 02:02.670
matching branches or not?

02:02.670 --> 02:03.990
But, we're just gonna go

02:03.990 --> 02:06.390
with require pull request reviews.

02:06.390 --> 02:08.280
So, Create.

02:08.280 --> 02:09.630
So now we have this branch rule

02:09.630 --> 02:11.460
that applies to one branch, main.

02:11.460 --> 02:13.080
It is protected.

02:13.080 --> 02:16.830
So, if I try and act as Stevie,

02:16.830 --> 02:18.570
so, I'm logged in as Stevie here

02:18.570 --> 02:21.300
and I want to make a change to the main branch.

02:21.300 --> 02:22.860
First of all, if I try,

02:22.860 --> 02:25.560
let's update even just the README,

02:25.560 --> 02:26.823
directly on main.

02:28.890 --> 02:30.090
I'm gonna start editing this.

02:30.090 --> 02:31.860
So, feature-branch-workflow.

02:31.860 --> 02:35.610
How about Bock Bock?

02:35.610 --> 02:37.380
Okay, I'm going to try

02:37.380 --> 02:38.610
and commit this.

02:38.610 --> 02:39.443
And take a look.

02:39.443 --> 02:41.130
It says you can't commit to main

02:41.130 --> 02:43.140
because it's a protected branch.

02:43.140 --> 02:45.960
Earlier, I showed an example of this

02:45.960 --> 02:46.793
and we could just commit

02:46.793 --> 02:48.750
directly to main, but now I can't.

02:48.750 --> 02:50.550
So, it wants me to make a new branch

02:50.550 --> 02:51.960
and start a pull request.

02:51.960 --> 02:54.030
So, I'm gonna do it just in the browser,

02:54.030 --> 02:55.470
instead of doing it locally.

02:55.470 --> 02:57.090
It would be the same exact process.

02:57.090 --> 02:58.530
Though, I'd make a feature branch,

02:58.530 --> 03:00.960
make my changes, push up the feature branch.

03:00.960 --> 03:03.450
So, this just makes me a feature branch

03:03.450 --> 03:04.560
and I use the default name

03:04.560 --> 03:07.110
it gave me StevieChicks-patch-1.

03:07.110 --> 03:07.950
All right.

03:07.950 --> 03:10.380
So, now I can make my PR

03:10.380 --> 03:12.940
from StevieChicks-patch-1 to main

03:13.800 --> 03:15.753
and I'm going to create that PR,

03:17.970 --> 03:19.680
but I can't merge it.

03:19.680 --> 03:21.420
Look, merging is blocked.

03:21.420 --> 03:24.240
Earlier, when we had made PRs as Stevie,

03:24.240 --> 03:26.910
I showed you that I could just merge it in myself.

03:26.910 --> 03:29.160
There's no real, there's nothing preventing me

03:29.160 --> 03:30.990
from doing it, aside from being a,

03:30.990 --> 03:33.510
I guess a trustworthy developer.

03:33.510 --> 03:34.740
I could make a PR

03:34.740 --> 03:36.750
that did something bad and broke master,

03:36.750 --> 03:39.270
or broke the main branch and just merge it in.

03:39.270 --> 03:42.180
But now, because of the protection rule we set up,

03:42.180 --> 03:45.270
we need, at least, one approving reviewer.

03:45.270 --> 03:47.820
So, I'm gonna go as Colt

03:47.820 --> 03:50.760
and be that approving reviewer, hopefully.

03:50.760 --> 03:52.383
So, here is that PR,

03:53.490 --> 03:55.170
it says it needs a review.

03:55.170 --> 03:57.150
So I can add it, if I want,

03:57.150 --> 03:58.890
or I'm an administrator, right?

03:58.890 --> 04:00.450
I'm the owner of this project,

04:00.450 --> 04:01.950
so I could just directly merge it.

04:01.950 --> 04:03.690
But I'm gonna add a review.

04:03.690 --> 04:05.340
So, adding a review is super simple.

04:05.340 --> 04:07.560
If I'm good with it, can click this.

04:07.560 --> 04:10.440
But I can also add, a note,

04:10.440 --> 04:13.140
a comment about things and say like,

04:13.140 --> 04:18.140
you know, "Always with the Bock Bock, Stevie?

04:21.360 --> 04:22.887
Get a new catchphrase."

04:23.940 --> 04:24.960
I'm joking around here,

04:24.960 --> 04:26.010
but you know,

04:26.010 --> 04:28.560
we can add things in, like that.

04:28.560 --> 04:29.970
We can then start a review.

04:29.970 --> 04:33.180
So, I can just add a single comment, if I want.

04:33.180 --> 04:35.880
Stevie will then be able to see that, over here.

04:35.880 --> 04:37.650
You can see it shows up for Stevie,

04:37.650 --> 04:38.483
I reviewed it.

04:38.483 --> 04:41.130
It says always blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.

04:41.130 --> 04:43.351
He can respond back to me.

04:43.351 --> 04:44.184
(keyboard clanking)

04:44.184 --> 04:45.423
Bock Bock Bock.

04:49.170 --> 04:50.970
Now, I go back to my side.

04:50.970 --> 04:52.833
I may need to refresh here.

04:53.820 --> 04:56.130
There, we see Stevie's response.

04:56.130 --> 04:58.710
Okay, so now, click Review Changes.

04:58.710 --> 05:02.160
I can finish the review and I can approve.

05:02.160 --> 05:03.930
So, I can approve merging the changes

05:03.930 --> 05:06.870
or I can request that he makes additional changes

05:06.870 --> 05:07.950
or I can just leave a comment

05:07.950 --> 05:10.050
without actually approving it.

05:10.050 --> 05:11.733
But I'm going to approve now.

05:14.490 --> 05:15.540
So, that was the review.

05:15.540 --> 05:17.070
It's still not merged in.

05:17.070 --> 05:19.770
So now, at least, one person has approved it,

05:19.770 --> 05:21.210
which is the rule we set up.

05:21.210 --> 05:22.290
You can have it be more,

05:22.290 --> 05:23.910
you can have two, three, four,

05:23.910 --> 05:26.250
however many people you need to approve it.

05:26.250 --> 05:28.290
There's all different fancy permission things

05:28.290 --> 05:29.123
you can get into,

05:29.123 --> 05:32.070
especially if you have an organization setup

05:32.070 --> 05:33.780
or an enterprise account.

05:33.780 --> 05:37.230
Anyway, now, I can merge that in here, right?

05:37.230 --> 05:38.520
That wasn't showing up before.

05:38.520 --> 05:39.390
So, I'm just gonna merge it.

05:39.390 --> 05:41.790
It's a very silly change to make

05:41.790 --> 05:43.750
and I'm gonna confirm that merge

05:45.090 --> 05:46.320
and that will close the PR.

05:46.320 --> 05:48.000
We can delete that branch.

05:48.000 --> 05:49.320
And now, the master branch

05:49.320 --> 05:53.190
that README, contains Bock Bock,

05:53.190 --> 05:54.810
at the very bottom.

05:54.810 --> 05:56.730
Okay, so silly little example.

05:56.730 --> 05:57.563
But, I wanted to show

05:57.563 --> 05:59.820
that we can set up these protection rules

05:59.820 --> 06:01.650
and they're very, very useful,

06:01.650 --> 06:04.170
especially, if you have a bunch of people working on,

06:04.170 --> 06:05.700
you know, one project together

06:05.700 --> 06:07.500
and they're making a lot of pull requests.

06:07.500 --> 06:08.333
And you want to be able

06:08.333 --> 06:09.900
to have some quality control

06:09.900 --> 06:12.090
or some feedback process, in place,

06:12.090 --> 06:13.590
where people can't just, you know,

06:13.590 --> 06:16.320
directly change the main branch.

06:16.320 --> 06:17.760
They, instead, are asked

06:17.760 --> 06:18.660
to make a pull request

06:18.660 --> 06:19.770
and then get feedback

06:19.770 --> 06:21.453
from at least one person.
